  "reason": "The strongest completed result is config_018, a multimodal multiprofile PCA + ResNet50 model with avgpool and concat fusion, reaching 0.6186 accuracy and 0.6103 F1, modestly above the best RNA-only multiprofile avgpool result. This suggests the current multimodal direction is promising, but fusion method is still untested: only concat has been evaluated. config_019 changes only the fusion from concat to weighted while keeping the same model, profile, RNA encoder, image encoder, and aggregation. It directly tests whether weighted fusion can improve on the best-known setting or whether concat is already sufficient. This is the best next use of budget because it exploits the strongest evidence while isolating one important design choice, giving both high expected performance and clear diagnostic value before exploring image encoders, aggregations, or alternative RNA encoders."
